 "structural_change": "MU-S81-2/HSLOT 10-19: RE-CLOSE of dsdv_mu_hslot (CLOSED view 28a8118d5) on the RTL of MU-S81-2/SEQ 5dd45e769: slot gap table -- each sel-0 f_mc boot word appends one gap g[k] (up to NSLOT 47 x 24 b), the slot timer walks g[0..n-1] cyclically with a registered prefetch, entries / pointers wrap at nw = n (one gap word = the former uniform period, nw = NSLOT). Needed because the record calendar is not uniform (AR gaps 21,312 / 21,316; MTP 10 x 124,524 + 58,160 filler): the closed uniform-S RTL raises t_mf[1] at user 3 on the real seq_host (f_uniform). Lead decision: keep the exact calendar of record incl. MTP filler, not the uniform-S alternative. Pins, faces, CSRs 0x15/0x16 and die wiring unchanged; +47x24 b gap table + ~40 control flops. Original kit: MU-S81/KIT 10-19 (NEW leaf, NSLOT 47 x {user 10, pos 21, due 32}, taps f_ks / f_kd beside dsdv_seq_host's L0, t_ku {v,user,pos} on the t_kd done edge, sticky faults t_mf).",
 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Source-registered: f_ks / f_kd / f_mc land in pin flops (ks_q / kd_q / mc_q), t_ku / t_mf leave flops."
 },
